// trap: a true rule whose proof needs two count lemmas past one row (#428). The rule reads
// only Shelf. Close needs at most two copies on the shelf and Crowd at least three; Stock
// adds a copy only to an open shelf and nothing removes one. So a closed shelf keeps at
// most two copies and a crowded one at least three: no shelf is closed and crowded, at any
// count. The rule is not inductive alone: from a closed shelf with three copies, which no
// reachable state has, Crowd breaks it. The facts that rule that state out count a shelf's
// copies. safety_count_guard_order.rdra is the same trap at one and two copies, which BFS
// reaches at the run's 2 instances; here no state at 2 instances has a third copy or a
// crowded shelf, so a count lemma has to come from the guards' bounds, not from the states.
// z3 proves the rule with the two count lemmas the guards give (#428), and BFS finds
// nothing.
// expect Forbidden_Shelf_0: native=ok tlc=ok z3=proved bfs=ok,ok,ok
entity Shelf "棚" {
  id: Int @pk
  status: Enum(open, closed) @default(open)
  crowded: Bool @default(false)
}
entity Copy "蔵書" { id: Int @pk }
usecase Build "棚設置"
usecase Stock "入架"
usecase Close "閉架"
usecase Crowd "混雑"
creates(Build, Shelf)
creates(Stock, Copy)
updates(Stock, Shelf)
transitions(Close, Shelf.status, open -> closed)
sets(Crowd, Shelf.crowded == true)
relate(Copy, Shelf, N:1)
condition ShelfOpen "開いている棚にだけ入架できる"
holds(ShelfOpen, Shelf.status == open)
applies_to(ShelfOpen, Stock)
condition FewCopies "蔵書が2冊以下の棚だけ閉架できる"
holds(FewCopies, Shelf.status == open).at_most(2, Copy)
applies_to(FewCopies, Close)
condition ManyCopies "蔵書が3冊以上の棚だけ混雑とする"
holds(ManyCopies, Shelf.crowded == false).at_least(3, Copy)
applies_to(ManyCopies, Crowd)
forbidden(Shelf, status == closed, crowded == true)
